# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_8021> (pergolide mesylate)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_8021> "A methanesulfonate salt obtained from pergolide by mixing eqimolar amount of pergolide and methanesulfonic acid. A dopamine D<small><sub>2</sub></small> receptor agonist which also has D<small><sub>1</sub></small> and D<small><sub>2</sub></small> agonist properties, it is used in the management of Parkinson's disease, although it was withdrawn from the U.S. and Canadian markets in 2007 due to an increased risk of cardiac valve dysfunction.")
