# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_81526> (endrin)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_81526> "An organochlorine compound resulting from the epoxidation of the double bond of isodrin. It is the <em>endo</em>, <em>endo</em> stereoisomer of dieldrin. It is an insecticide mainly used on field crops such as cotton and grains and has also been used as a rodenticide to control mice and voles. The product is banned in many countries since it is a persistent organic pollutant.")
